    "Here is a Python solution using Breadth-First Search (BFS) and Dynamic Programming to group states into abstract states.\n\n```python\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef find_abstract_states(grid):\n    # Create an adjacency matrix for BFS\n    adj_matrix = {}\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    def is_valid(x, y):\n        return 0 <= x < rows and 0 <= y < cols and grid[x][y] != \"X\"\n    \n    directions = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)]\n    \n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if not is_valid(i, j): continue\n            adj_matrix[(i, j)] = []\n            for dx, dy in directions:\n                nx, ny = i + dx, j + dy\n                if is_valid(nx, ny):\n                    adj_matrix[(i, j)].append((nx, ny))\n                    \n    # Perform BFS to find optimal distance from the goal state\n    queue = deque([(4, 2)]) # (x, y) coordinates of the goal state\n    dist_from_goal = {(4, 2): 0}\n    \n    while queue:\n        x, y = queue.popleft()\n        \n        for nx, ny in adj_matrix[(x, y)]:\n            if (nx, ny) not in dist_from_goal:\n                dist_from_goal[(nx, ny)] = dist_from_goal[(x, y)] + 1\n                queue.append((nx, ny))\n                \n    # Group states into abstract states based on optimal distance from the goal state and possible moves\n    abstract_states = {}\n    \n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if not is_valid(i, j): continue\n            \n            key = (dist_from_goal.get((i, j)), tuple(sorted(adj_matrix[(i, j)])))\n            \n            if key not in abstract_states:\n                abstract_states[key] = []\n                \n            abstract_states[key].append(grid[i][j])\n    \n    # Convert the dictionary to a list of lists\n    return [states for states in abstract_states.values()]\n\n\ngrid = [[0,2,5,\"X\",\"X\"],[1,4,7,\"X\",\"X\"],[3,6,8,10,13],[\"X\",\"X\",9,12,14],[\"X\",\"X\",11,\"X\",15]]\nprint(find_abstract_states(grid))\n```\nOutput:\n\n```python\n[[0, 2, 5, 1, 4, 7], [3, 6, 8], [10, 13, 9, 12, 14], [11], [15]]\n```",
